# Waiver list for `scripts/check-convention-import-uniqueness.pl`.
#
# Each row pins the dominant FQCN for a Java simple class name. The dominant
# FQCN is the one that *should* be imported anywhere it's needed; any other
# FQCN sharing the same simple name must be referenced via its fully-qualified
# name inline (never imported).
#
# Format:  <SimpleName>  <whitespace>  <dominant.FQCN>
# Comments start with `#` and run to end of line. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# When a row is present here, the checker:
#  - suppresses the dominant-FQCN side of the conflict from the report (those
#    imports are correct);
#  - flags only the non-dominant FQCN imports, with their file paths, so the
#    report is focused on actionable cleanup.
#
# Special FQCN value `*` means "intentionally polysemous, accept any number
# of FQCNs for this simple name". Use sparingly — only for names that
# legitimately mean different things across modules with no chance of
# conflation (e.g. `Field` from java.lang.reflect vs org.jooq vs Apache Arrow:
# different domains, different files, no risk of confusion).
#
# When a simple name is NOT in this list and has 2+ distinct FQCNs in the
# repo, every variant is reported (no canonical pick has been declared yet).
#
# To add a new pin: pick the dominant FQCN by majority usage today, declare it
# below, run the checker, and clean up the non-dominant imports it lists.

Builder        lombok.Builder
Configuration  org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration
ImmutableMap   com.google.common.collect.ImmutableMap
Logger         org.slf4j.Logger
Mode           org.openjdk.jmh.annotations.Mode
Nullable       org.jspecify.annotations.Nullable
Supplier       java.util.function.Supplier
Suppliers      com.google.common.base.Suppliers
Table          org.jooq.Table
Throwables     com.google.common.base.Throwables
Value          lombok.Value

# Intentionally polysemous — distinct domains, no risk of conflation.
# Cross-library names where each FQCN means a fundamentally different concept:
Document       *
EventBus       *
Expression     *
Field          *
Level          *
Param          *
ParseException *
Schema         *
Subscribe      *
Util           *

# `NonNull` serves two distinct purposes that should both stay reachable:
#  - `lombok.NonNull` adds a runtime null-check in Lombok-generated code (constructor, builder,
#    setter), with the exception type configured by `lombok.config:lombok.nonNull.exceptionType`.
#  - `org.jspecify.annotations.NonNull` is compile-only nullness for static analysis (NullAway,
#    IDE highlights, NullMarked package semantics).
# Per <https://github.com/projectlombok/lombok/issues/3865>, jspecify is intentionally compile-only
# and should not be treated as a synonym for `@lombok.NonNull` at the runtime layer. Each codebase
# position picks the form that matches its intent (runtime guard vs static-analysis hint).
NonNull        *

# Webflux vs webmvc framework split — both modules legitimately need their own framework's class:
CsrfToken                   *
ResourceHandlerRegistration *
ResourceHandlerRegistry     *
